{# Route registry lives in src/_data/site.json. `nav: false` on the home entry is why it is absent
here: home is reachable via the h1 link, exactly as it is today. NOTE: keep angle brackets out of
these Nunjucks comments. Prettier's HTML printer parses tag names inside them as real markup and
mangles the file. YEO-139: home canonicalises to origin + "/", not /index.html. YEO-140: emit
aria-current="page" when p.key == key, and wrap these bare list items in a ul (they are invalid as
direct nav children today; preserved as-is so this PR stays a pure port). #}
<nav id="site-nav">
    {%- for p in site.pages %}{% if p.nav %}
    <li><a href="{{ p.url }}">{{ p.label }}</a></li>
    {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
</nav>
